From: Neo <neo@Neos-MacBook.local>
Date: Sat, 15 Aug 2026 10:02:44 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 04/11] adopt int_const_hoist from levkropp, gated to AArch64
 (x86 would regress)

Lev's pass (e896ab2b) hoists integer constants outside A64 imm12/cmn
encoding range out of loop bodies into preheader Copies - on AArch64
each such constant otherwise costs movz+movk per iteration (sieve's
marking-loop bound).

CRITICAL DIVERGENCE from his version: he registers the pass
unconditionally. On x86-64 any imm32 encodes directly into cmp/add, so
hoisting is a strict pessimization there - measured on sieve -O2:
'cmpq $10000000, %r11' became a register compare, burned %r10, and
added a callee-saved push to the prologue. Gated to
Target::Aarch64 only.

