From 542bce2284cc73109d914f8dd425db05a5444752 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arena Agent <agent@arena.ai>
Date: Sat, 15 Aug 2026 21:54:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 05/11] adopt AArch64 fused FP compare-and-branch from
 levkropp, hardened
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Backport of fef5e2d1: FP comparisons feeding a CondBranch materialized a
cset boolean and branched on it (fcmp; cset; mov; cbz = 4 insns per FP
branch in mandelbrot's escape test). detect_cmp_branch_fusion now (a)
accepts float compares on backends whose emit_fused_cmp_branch handles
them (new supports_fused_fp_cmp_branch hook, AArch64-only), (b) also
fuses across a dead phi-web Copy between the Cmp and the branch, with
strict use-count proofs for both shapes (Copy dead + cmp_uses==2, or
Copy single-use + cmp_uses==1).

TWO DIVERGENCES from Lev's version:
1. BUG IN HIS VERSION FIXED: he gates FP fusion on ty.is_float() alone.
   long double lowers to soft-float libcalls on AArch64; routing F128
   through a d-register fcmp reads half the value — his tip MISCOMPILES
   glibc_ld_builtins (sqrtl(9.0L)==3.0L fails). Fusion is restricted to
   hardware F32/F64.
2. Program-point alignment: our skip paths bump current_program_point
   for both the fused Cmp AND the skipped dead Copy (liveness numbers
   every IR instruction; his version silently desynced the point).

The ARM emitter's fcmp cond-code map (mi/ls for lt/le) is byte-identical
to emit_float_cmp_impl's cset map, so NaN-unordered semantics are
preserved exactly.

PROOF:
- mandelbrot kernel: cset 4 -> 1, qemu output 15477 == native gcc -O2.
- NaN matrix test (14 compares incl. n==n, n!=n): 10277 == gcc.
- glibc_ld_builtins passes (fails on lev/main tip).
- x86 asm BIT-IDENTICAL (hook returns false); 162/162 x86 regression,
  653 lib tests, ARM differential at baseline 91.
