From c328119b6ceba77f69fafefcea2d95006c673d48 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arena Agent <agent@arena.ai>
Date: Sat, 15 Aug 2026 22:02:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 06/11] adopt multi-pair phi coalescing + FP no-op copy elision
 from levkropp

Backport of 94141751 in three coordinated parts:

1. detect_phi_coalesce_groups returns ALL loop-block Copy pairs per phi
   dest instead of only the first found. The first-found rule meant a
   loop-entry copy (acc <- init) shadowed the true backedge copy
   (acc <- updated), so the accumulator update kept a register-to-
   register shuffle in the loop body. Soundness shifts to the consumers,
   which all carry per-pair proofs: register propagation revalidates the
   same-block def/copy window and rejects interval conflicts (later
   pairs see earlier pairs' assignments in the shared map and fail
   closed); the ARM FP-coalesce pass has its own conflict check.

2. copy_coalescing: one NEW slot alias per phi dest (claimed_dests set).
   Slot aliasing has no per-source interval conflict check, so two
   backedge sources sharing one dest slot could observe each other's
   writes - this claim set is the multi-pair enabler for the slot path.

3. ARM emit: promoted-F64 copies where FP phi coalescing assigned src
   and dest registers skip the d0 round-trip (fmov d0, dN; fmov dN, d0
   becomes nothing when same reg, one direct fmov otherwise).

PROOF: x86 asm verified BIT-IDENTICAL on phi-heavy tests
(loop_alloca_scalar, reduction_two_sums); 240/240 differential fuzz vs
gcc; 653 lib, 162/162 x86 regression, 50/50 correctness, 3/3
intrinsics; ARM differential at baseline 91; conditional FP accumulator
loop prints 2.000000 == native gcc -O2 under qemu.
