Backport of 90e05e19. Two independent wins:

1. FP register pool: was caller-saved d16-d23 (+d24-d31 promotion pool)
   only, so FP-heavy code with >8-16 live values spilled temporaries
   GCC keeps in registers. d8-d14 (allocator IDs 32-38) join the scan,
   appended AFTER the caller-saved pool so the free registers fill
   first; prologue/epilogue save/restore only the ones actually
   assigned (stp/ldp pairs + odd tail). d15/v15 stays reserved (FMA
   intrinsic scratch). is_arm_fp_phys, the FP phi-coalesce filter, and
   arm_fp_name all extended to the 32..=38 range. CCC_NO_FP_CALLEE_SAVED
   opt-out for A/B.

2. emit_gep_reg_const hook (default false): when a constant-offset GEP
   has base AND dest register-assigned, AArch64 emits one add/sub
   dest, base, #imm instead of the mov-to-x0 + add + mov-back
   round-trip that every pointer-marching loop paid per iteration.

