From 970e3e08902eacc72bc974a98b3a5e4c2251b8a8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arena Agent <agent@arena.ai>
Date: Sat, 15 Aug 2026 22:25:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 09/11] fix reduction vectorizer: reject IV-dependent GEP bases
 (OOB segfault)

PRE-EXISTING MISCOMPILE on upstream main, found while stress-testing the
iv_strength_reduce stride limit with a 256x256 matmul whose result is
consumed via a diagonal sum:

    double s=0; for (i=0;i<N;i++) s += C[i][i];

lowers to a two-level GEP chain:
    row  = C + (i << 11)      ; base DEPENDS ON i
    addr = row + (i << 3)     ; offset alone looks like stride-8

detect: gep_uses_iv only inspected the OFFSET operand. The transform then
models the access as invariant_base + iv*8, rewrites the IV to step in
BYTES (0,32,...,2047), and keeps all other IV uses - so the row term
becomes C + (byte_iv << 11), up to 4 MB past C. SIGSEGV at runtime;
every gate except CCC_DISABLE_PASSES=vectorize left the crash in place,
and origin/main (730ccabd) reproduces it verbatim.

FIX: gep_uses_iv now requires the GEP BASE to be loop-invariant via the
new gep_base_is_loop_invariant helper - defined outside the loop, or a
constant address (GlobalAddr/Alloca), following Copy chains, everything
else fails closed. Contiguous reductions are untouched.

PROOF:
- vectorize_iv_dependent_base.c: diagonal + strided-diagonal sums, both
  previously SIGSEGV, now exact (32640/16256); added to regression.
- Legit patterns still fire: 'Reduction pattern matched' for s+=a[i]
  and dot product, outputs equal gcc -O2 (4193280 / 196561).
- 653 lib, 163/163 x86 regression, ARM 92 (test passes there too),
  240/240 differential fuzz.
