Date: Sat, 15 Aug 2026 22:28:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 10/11] adopt IVSR stride limit 1024 -> 1 MiB from levkropp
 (2b555fbc slice)

Matrix row strides are routinely several KiB (256 doubles = 2048 bytes)
and their multiply executes in the ENCLOSING hot loop, so excluding them
from pointer induction left an imul + re-addressing on the middle-loop
path of every ikj matmul.

ADOPTION ORDER MATTERS: applied only AFTER the reduction vectorizer's
IV-dependent-base fix (previous commit). On the unfixed compiler this
same stride bump turns the latent vectorizer OOB into a hard segfault
on 256x256 matmul + diagonal sum - which is exactly how the upstream
bug was flushed out. Lev's tree carries the same latent combination.

PROOF: 384x384 ikj matmul x3, best-of-2: 0.303s -> 0.288s (~5%) on
x86-64; result identical; 653 lib, 163/163 x86 regression, ARM 92,
240/240 differential fuzz. (gcc -O2 remains 5.6x faster on this kernel
- full loop-nest vectorization is tracked as future work, not a
regression.)
